            <ArticleTitle>The needle in a haystack: appropriate use of interventional techniques in the management of chronic pain.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>215-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Management of chronic pain is often difficult. Interventional approaches, such as joint injections and nerve blocks, can reduce dependence on opioid therapy, polypharmacy, and long-term costs; they can also dramatically improve pain control and function. However, interventional techniques must be used ethically and judiciously as part of a comprehensive approach to patient-centered care.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
